\section{Evaluation}

In order to evaluate our system we carried out experiments on a variety of test datasets. To determine which method would be the most successful in carrying out the tasks we wanted to carry out, we carried out ablation studies in which we tested each different component.

\subsection{Training Datasets}
We had four datasets to work with:

\subsubsection{Wikipedia:}
This was used as a source for creating the sentence embedding dataset. The sentences were collected using the Wikipedia's \texttt{randompage} module.

\subsection{The Simplification Task}
We now define the simplification task. The input to the task is a sentence, and the output is its simplified version.
We follow the definition of \citet{xu-etal-2016-optimizing} and formulate the simplification task as a rewrite process in which a given sentence is rewritten to a simpler version with no more than 5\% of tokens from the original sentence being modified. We define this criterion as the \textit{token penalty}, denoted by $\rho$.

