\textbf{Topic Classification:} Given a topic classification task and a set of sentences $D$ where each sentence is assigned to one or more of the topic classifications, the objective is to train a classifier that is able to predict the class labels of unlabeled sentences.

\begin{enumerate}
\item

Topic classification as an NLP task can be done using a variety of classifiers such as Na\"ive Bayes classifiers, SVMs, Decision trees, Logistic regression and Neural networks.

 This challenge is very similar to the one-line text simplification challenge proposed by \citet{zhang2017sentence}, with the key differences being that the input text is longer and the response is much shorter than in that work.

